    -> OPPOSITE SIGNS. Promoter and non-promoter methylation 
       relate to expression in opposite directions, which is 
       the textbook promoter-versus-gene-body pattern and is 
       evidence that the signal is promoter-specific. 

== 6. Within-stratum consistency =============================== 
  RASSF9 promoter methylation and expression both differ by tumour 
  site, so an association driven entirely by that split would be a 
  between-group artefact rather than a within-tumour relationship. 
  RASSF9   T2 / Metastatic                      n = 311 | rho = -0.341, p = 6.74e-10   | adj beta = -1.322 [-1.835, -0.809], p = 6.96e-07 
  RASSF9   T2 / Primary Tumor                   n = 100 | rho = -0.418, p = 1.54e-05   | adj beta = -1.051 [-1.682, -0.420], p = 0.001 
  RASSF10  T2 / Metastatic                      n = 311 | rho = -0.144, p = 0.011      | adj beta = -0.991 [-1.475, -0.507], p = 7.04e-05 
  RASSF10  T2 / Primary Tumor                   n = 100 | rho = -0.147, p = 0.145      | adj beta = -1.441 [-3.088, 0.207], p = 0.086 
 
  -> the association must hold INSIDE each stratum, not only 
     across them, for the silencing interpretation to stand 

