== 8. Reading this ============================================= 
  WHAT WOULD MAKE THIS A STRONG VALIDATION: 
    - the effect size holds across tiers, not just the p value 
    - promoter probes behave differently from non-promoter probes 
    - the association survives within primary and within metastatic 
    - it is present in the samples the original filter excluded 
 
  WHAT WOULD UNDERCUT IT: 
    - every probe on the locus correlates equally, which would point 
      at a sample-level property (purity, cell composition) rather 
      than promoter silencing 
    - the association disappears within strata 
 
  NOT TESTED HERE: uveal melanoma, which would be the ideal non-UV 
  control, is a separate GDC project (TCGA-UVM) and is not in these 
  cohort files. It needs its own download and script. 
  no warnings raised 
